       delpart - tell the kernel to forget about a partition

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ddeellppaarrtt _d_e_v_i_c_e _p_a_r_t_i_t_i_o_n

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ddeellppaarrtt asks the Linux kernel to forget about the specified _p_a_r_t_i_t_i_o_n
       (a number) on the specified _d_e_v_i_c_e. The command is a simple wrapper
       around the "del partition" ioctl.

       This command doesn’t manipulate partitions on a block device.

